# Providers and Automation

## Providers

All hypervisor ops go through `lib/providers/base.py`.

- `libvirt.py` — KVM/QEMU (v1)
- `hyperv.py` — Hyper-V (local/remote; Nest control via SSH by default — #218)
- Nest control plane: `lib/nest_transport.py` — SSH default (key **reference**); WinRM Nest fallback (#220)
- Guest provision stays in `lib/provision.py` (WinRM for Windows guests)

```
❌ Add a method to BaseProvider "just in case" or for one provider only
✅ Implement in the Nest provider using existing BaseProvider methods;
   extend base.py only if every provider must support it
❌ Put Nest WinRM/SSH session code in provision.py — use nest_transport for Nest hosts
```

Docs: [`.hatchery/docs/nest-transport.md`](../../.hatchery/docs/nest-transport.md).

## Answer files

Request by OS type via `lib/answerfile.py` — it picks the strategy. Templates: `templates/answerfiles/` (`win10`, `win11`, `server2022`, `server2025`).

```
❌ Hardcode Autounattend paths in the Flask route
✅ Call answerfile helpers; add a new guest = new template + branch in answerfile.py
```

Win11 / Server 2025 need UEFI + TPM (`swtpm`).

## Provisioning

`lib/provision.py`: WinRM for Windows; SSH later for Linux.

